  "reason": "Evidence: config_038 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) is our best result at 0.721 acc, substantially above RNA-only best (0.653) and image-only (0.208), confirming that fusion of a strong RNA encoder with a strong image encoder is highly beneficial. However, we have only tested one fusion strategy (concat) in the multimodal setting. Question: config_039 is identical to config_038 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, isolating the effect of fusion strategy on the best-performing configuration. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a clean single-variable comparison that directly tests whether the interaction between modalities benefits from learned weighting versus simple concatenation. If weighted fusion improves performance, it signals that modality importance is non-uniform and we should prioritize fusion design; if it does not, concat is sufficient and we can redirect budget toward other axes (e.g., aggregation or RNA encoder choice in the multimodal setting). This is the highest-information, lowest-risk next step given the limited budget."
